Changes
=======

2.0.0 UNRELEASED
   * v2 is not tagged yet; this entry documents work in progress on the
     develop/v2 branch, not a shipped release.
   - Module path moved to github.com/lestrrat-go/server-starter/v2
   - The listener subpackage is folded into the module root (package
     starter); import the module root instead of a listener subpackage
   - The supervisor is no longer importable as a Go library. It ships only
     as the start_server command; programs that embedded the supervisor
     should run the compiled binary as a subprocess instead
   - start_server rejects unknown --signal-on-hup and --signal-on-term names
     instead of silently using TERM; XFSZ is now recognized correctly
   - Added worker-facing helpers: ParsePorts, NewTCPListener, NewUDPListener,
     NewUnixListener, Generation, IsUnderStartServer, and a new UDPListener
     type with ListenPacketAll for UDP support
   - Three deliberate behavior changes, introduced in v2, relative to the
     original Perl Server::Starter:
     * On receiving INT or QUIT, the supervisor now sends the worker the
       same signal configured via --signal-on-term that it already sends on
       TERM, instead of a hardcoded TERM. Only observable when
       --signal-on-term is set to something other than TERM and the
       supervisor is stopped with INT or QUIT rather than TERM.
     * When a file is deleted from the envdir, the corresponding
       environment variable no longer keeps the last value the supervisor
       applied from it; it falls back to the value inherited from the real
       environment, since the worker's environment is now built fresh on
       every spawn.
     * KILL_OLD_DELAY, ENABLE_AUTO_RESTART, and AUTO_RESTART_INTERVAL are no
       longer exported into the supervisor's own process environment. They
       are passed as configuration instead, so command-line values are not
       newly exported to workers. Ambient and envdir values retain their
       normal worker inheritance, with envdir values taking precedence.
   - See MIGRATION.md for a full symbol-by-symbol migration guide

0.0.2 Jan 06 2015
   - Check if given command is executable before starting start_server
   - Add support for unix domain sockets (kazeburo)

0.0.1 Jan 05 2015
   - Initial release
